Nodes 3
Tiers 2
Podsize 3

# The cx5_100g_3node topology at the declared ConnectX-7 rate. Geometry and
# per-hop latency are identical, so the two profiles differ in link rate
# alone, which is what "the same architecture at a higher rate" has to mean
# for the two curves to be comparable.
#
# The rate is the scaled profile goodput asymptote rounded to whole Gbit/s,
# which is what the loader parses and what the runtime requires -link_bps to
# match. At this rate the four store-and-forward serializations shrink by four
# while the four pipe traversals do not, so the emergent message offset is
# expected about 11 percent below the 100 G one rather than equal to it.
Tier 0
Downlink_speed_Gbps 388
Radix_Down 3
Radix_Up 3
Downlink_Latency_ns 515
Switch_Latency_ns 0

# Three spine switches, each with one link to the leaf.
Tier 1
Downlink_speed_Gbps 388
Radix_Down 1
Downlink_Latency_ns 515
Switch_Latency_ns 0
